factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 3 problems
  The caption's 'மக்கள் கவனத்திற்கு' line adds an advisory (don't throw garbage in hospital premises) that is not stated in the article as a message to the public; the article only says public-thrown tea cups and plastic cause blockages, which is a claim of cause, not an instruction.
  The caption says the hospital administration's explanation was given, but the reel_script and slides say 'மருத்துவமனை நிர்வாகம் விழிப்புணர்வு ஏற்படுத்தவில்லை என மக்கள் கேள்வி எழுப்பினர்' - the article says public members talked among themselves wondering whether the administration does not create awareness; 'கேள்வி எழுப்பினர்' (raised questions) overstates this as a public demand, and the slide line 'மருத்துவமனை நிர்வாகம் விளக்கம் அளித்தது' (hospital administration gave an explanation) is loosely attributed to the administration rather than the RMO Saravanapriya.
  The reel_script says 'பொதுப்பணித்துறை முன்வரவில்லை' is a complaint by staff, which is accurate, but the reel_script and caption say 'ஊழியர்கள் குற்றம் சாட்டினர்' - acceptable; however the caption omits the staff's statement that the pipe is in the ground near the visitor seating area, not a fact needing change.
